# Byte-exact checkouts on every platform: dsl_hash and corpus_hash are sha256 over file bytes,
# so CRLF conversion on a Windows clone would silently break the golden vectors.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Hash-bearing fixtures are BYTES: no eol conversion in either direction, so a working copy whose bytes differ
# from the blob (a CRLF file written by a Windows tool) shows up in `git status` instead of being normalised
# silently at commit while the working copy keeps the CR (found 2026-09-20: step 5 gave 92/9 instead of 98/3).
contracts/golden/** -text
learning/fixtures/** -text
drafts/** -text
*.log -text
*.png binary
*.gz binary
